</edge>
<edge source="E:Concept:explainable_ai" target="E:Concept:interpretability" id="1">
  <data key="d4">RELATED_TO</data>
  <data key="d5">KDJ-AI-2026E1-P04-C30-S04-1BD83495</data>
  <data key="d6">source</data>
  <data key="d7">NIST-IR-8367::P0029::SEC3.2::B0148</data>
  <data key="d8">the concepts of interpretability and explainability are 'closely related'</data>
</edge>
<edge source="E:Concept:explainable_ai" target="E:EvaluationMethod:human_benchmark" id="0">
  <data key="d4">MEASURED_BY</data>
  <data key="d5">KDJ-AI-2026E1-P04-C29-S10-CDFE093D</data>
  <data key="d6">source</data>
  <data key="d7">NIST-IR-8312::P0029::SEC9::B0177</data>
  <data key="d8">humans demonstrate only limited ability to meet the principles outlined here. This provides a benchmark</data>
</edge>
<edge source="E:Concept:explainable_ai" target="E:Concept:trust_in_ai_systems" id="0">
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTED_BY</data>
  <data key="d5">KDJ-AI-2026E1-P04-C29-S10-CDFE093D</data>
  <data key="d6">source</data>
  <data key="d7">NIST-IR-8312::P0029::SEC9::B0179</data>
  <data key="d8">Explainable AI contributes to the safe operation and trust of multiple facets of complex AI systems.</data>
</edge>
