<edge source="E:Mitigation:adversarial_training" target="E:Attack:evasion_attack" id="0">
  <data key="d4">MITIGATES</data>
  <data key="d5">KDJ-AI-2026E1-P03-C20-S07-3B73DC25</data>
  <data key="d6">source</data>
  <data key="d7">NIST-AI-100-2E2025::P0024::SECNISTAML022BACKTOINDEX::B0162</data>
  <data key="d8">The most promising directions for mitigating the critical threat of evasion attacks are adversarial training</data>
</edge>
<edge source="E:Mitigation:adversarial_training" target="E:Attack:evasion_attack" id="1">
  <data key="d4">MITIGATES</data>
  <data key="d5">KDJ-AI-2026E1-P03-C20-S12-EC9735A3</data>
  <data key="d6">source</data>
  <data key="d7">NIST-AI-100-2E2025::P0030::SEC2.2.5::B0199</data>
  <data key="d8">adversarial training is a general method that augments training data with adversarial examples</data>
</edge>
<edge source="E:Mitigation:adversarial_training" target="E:Risk:robustness_accuracy_tradeoff" id="0">
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d5">KDJ-AI-2026E1-P03-C20-S07-3B73DC25</data>
  <data key="d6">source</data>
  <data key="d7">NIST-AI-100-2E2025::P0024::SECNISTAML022BACKTOINDEX::B0162</data>
  <data key="d8">there is an inherent tradeoff between robustness and accuracy</data>
</edge>
<edge source="E:Mitigation:adversarial_training" target="E:Risk:robustness_accuracy_trade_off" id="0">
  <data key="d4">AFFECTS</data>
  <data key="d5">KDJ-AI-2026E1-P03-C20-S12-EC9735A3</data>
  <data key="d6">source</data>
  <data key="d7">NIST-AI-100-2E2025::P0030::SEC2.2.5::B0199</data>
  <data key="d8">this benefit usually comes at the cost of decreased model accuracy on clean data</data>
</edge>
